# CVE-2024-58103 (CWE-400/CWE-674): Wire's protobuf reader recursed into
# nested groups without any depth budget. `skipGroup` walks a
# START_GROUP/END_GROUP-delimited section of the input, and its
# STATE_START_GROUP arm handles a nested group by calling itself:
#
#   STATE_START_GROUP -> skipGroup(tag) // Nested group.
#
# Each `0xa3 0x01` byte pair in the attacker's message opens one more
# group, so 50KB of crafted input costs 25000 native stack frames and the
# decoding process dies of a stack overflow. The same two files carry the
# fix (b90e60c "Enforce recursion limit on nested groups",
# ProtoReader.kt and ByteArrayProtoReader32.kt): the arm becomes a block
# that increments `recursionDepth`, throws past `RECURSION_LIMIT`, and
# decrements in a `finally`.
#
# The discriminating fact is not the recursion itself but its asymmetry
# with the rest of the class. `ProtoReader` owns a depth budget:
# `recursionDepth` is declared beside the cursors, `RECURSION_LIMIT = 100`
# sits in the companion, and `beginMessage` enforces it with the very
# same `if (++recursionDepth > RECURSION_LIMIT) throw IOException("Wire
# recursion limit exceeded")` the fixed revision copies. A message's nesting is
# budgeted; a group's nesting is not, and the group path is reached from
# `nextTag` for every unknown field of that encoding. Both revisions
# carry the budget and the self-call, so no fact naming either alone
# separates them -- only "the self-recursive call site consults the
# budget" does.
#
# ATTENTION. Nothing reports on either revision, and the first blocker is
# an extraction defect the engine fix shipped with this spec removes:
#
# 1. A brace-less `when` arm had no lowering. `ktWhen` collected an
#    entry's body only when it arrived as a `block`,
#    `control_structure_body` or `statements` node, and tree-sitter-kotlin
#    wraps a braced body in a `block` but leaves `1 -> skipGroup(tag)`
#    as a bare `call_expression`. Every brace-less arm's code drops out
#    -- including the self-call this CVE turns on, which produced no node
#    at all (`vyql graph` on the vulnerable `skipGroup` showed the
#    `internalReadVarint32` call and nothing inside the `when`). The
#    fourth test holds the isolating pair: the same `FileInputStream`
#    arm reported VYQL-RES-001 braced and nothing unbraced, and 262
#    further brace-less statement-position arms across 70 Kotlin files in
#    the reachable clones are equally invisible. `when` in expression
#    position (`return when (x) { ... }`) is never affected -- `expr()`
#    flattens it through a `Seq` and keeps the calls. Lowering a bare arm
#    through `c.stmt` makes it reachable and is measured below.
#
# 2. With the arm lowered, the self-call exists and still reports
#    nothing, which is the depth-budget family recorded for C
#    (1320, libzmq), JS (1391, 1262 KaTeX), Rust (1697, rulex) and
#    Kotlin's missing CWE-400 classifier (1255, kaml). Two facts are
#    missing together. No predicate unifies two context values, so "this
#    function calls itself" does not compile (`node.context.name ==
#    node.context.call` is rejected because presence predicates take
#    string literals only); and the Kotlin frontend emits no
#    `analysis.function.context` node at all -- `kotlin.go` never sets
#    `ContextTokens`, so there is no function- or class-scoped token set
#    in which the question could even be asked. The budget asymmetry
#    needs class-member scope (`beginMessage`'s check read against
#    `skipGroup`'s arm), which the same omission makes unreachable.
#
# Naming `skipGroup` or `recursionDepth` in a binding would key on this
# fix's own shape rather than on any documented API -- `skipGroup` is a
# private implementation detail with no public surface, and the counter
# is present at both revisions -- so no definition change shipped for the
# finding itself.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap
# Tests one and two stay quiet on both revisions until recursion-depth
# budget vocabulary lands. Tests three and four both expect, now that a
# brace-less when arm lowers like its braced form.

test "rank1954: skipGroup re-enters itself for every nested group with no depth budget"
  lang kotlin
  file wire-runtime/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/squareup/wire/ProtoReader.kt
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject VYQL-DOS-042
  reject VYQL-DOS-045
  code
  ```
  import okio.BufferedSource

  open class ProtoReader(private val source: BufferedSource) {
    private var pos: Long = 0
    private var limit = Long.MAX_VALUE
    private var state = STATE_LENGTH_DELIMITED

    /** The current number of levels of message nesting. */
    private var recursionDepth = 0

    @Throws(IOException::class)
    open fun beginMessage(): Long {
      check(state == STATE_LENGTH_DELIMITED) { "Unexpected call to beginMessage()" }
      if (++recursionDepth > RECURSION_LIMIT) {
        throw IOException("Wire recursion limit exceeded")
      }
      state = STATE_TAG
      return pushedLimit
    }

    open fun nextTag(): Int {
      loop@ while (pos < limit && !source.exhausted()) {
        val tagAndFieldEncoding = internalReadVarint32()
        if (tagAndFieldEncoding == 0) throw ProtocolException("Unexpected tag 0")
        tag = tagAndFieldEncoding shr TAG_FIELD_ENCODING_BITS
        when (val groupOrFieldEncoding = tagAndFieldEncoding and FIELD_ENCODING_MASK) {
          STATE_START_GROUP -> {
            skipGroup(tag)
            continue@loop
          }
          STATE_END_GROUP -> throw ProtocolException("Unexpected end group")
          STATE_LENGTH_DELIMITED -> {
            internalNextLengthDelimited()
            return tag
          }
          else -> throw ProtocolException("Unexpected field encoding: $groupOrFieldEncoding")
        }
      }
      return -1
    }

    /** Skips a section of the input delimited by START_GROUP/END_GROUP type markers. */
    private fun skipGroup(expectedEndTag: Int) {
      while (pos < limit && !source.exhausted()) {
        val tagAndFieldEncoding = internalReadVarint32()
        if (tagAndFieldEncoding == 0) throw ProtocolException("Unexpected tag 0")
        val tag = tagAndFieldEncoding shr TAG_FIELD_ENCODING_BITS
        when (val groupOrFieldEncoding = tagAndFieldEncoding and FIELD_ENCODING_MASK) {
          STATE_START_GROUP -> skipGroup(tag) // Nested group.
          STATE_END_GROUP -> {
            if (tag == expectedEndTag) return // Success!
            throw ProtocolException("Unexpected end group")
          }
          STATE_LENGTH_DELIMITED -> {
            val length = internalReadVarint32()
            pos += length.toLong()
            source.skip(length.toLong())
          }
          else -> throw ProtocolException("Unexpected field encoding: $groupOrFieldEncoding")
        }
      }
      throw EOFException("Expected a containing end group but reached the end of the input")
    }

    internal companion object {
      internal const val RECURSION_LIMIT = 100
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1954: the fixed revision bounds every nested group against the reader's own recursion limit"
  lang kotlin
  file wire-runtime/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/squareup/wire/ProtoReader.kt
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject VYQL-DOS-042
  reject VYQL-DOS-045
  code
  ```
  import okio.BufferedSource

  open class ProtoReader(private val source: BufferedSource) {
    private var pos: Long = 0
    private var limit = Long.MAX_VALUE
    private var state = STATE_LENGTH_DELIMITED

    /** The current number of levels of message nesting. */
    private var recursionDepth = 0

    @Throws(IOException::class)
    open fun beginMessage(): Long {
      check(state == STATE_LENGTH_DELIMITED) { "Unexpected call to beginMessage()" }
      if (++recursionDepth > RECURSION_LIMIT) {
        throw IOException("Wire recursion limit exceeded")
      }
      state = STATE_TAG
      return pushedLimit
    }

    /** Skips a section of the input delimited by START_GROUP/END_GROUP type markers. */
    private fun skipGroup(expectedEndTag: Int) {
      while (pos < limit && !source.exhausted()) {
        val tagAndFieldEncoding = internalReadVarint32()
        if (tagAndFieldEncoding == 0) throw ProtocolException("Unexpected tag 0")
        val tag = tagAndFieldEncoding shr TAG_FIELD_ENCODING_BITS
        when (val groupOrFieldEncoding = tagAndFieldEncoding and FIELD_ENCODING_MASK) {
          STATE_START_GROUP -> {
            recursionDepth++
            try {
              if (recursionDepth > RECURSION_LIMIT) {
                throw IOException("Wire recursion limit exceeded")
              }
              // Nested group.
              skipGroup(tag)
            } finally {
              recursionDepth--
            }
          }
          STATE_END_GROUP -> {
            if (tag == expectedEndTag) return // Success!
            throw ProtocolException("Unexpected end group")
          }
          STATE_LENGTH_DELIMITED -> {
            val length = internalReadVarint32()
            pos += length.toLong()
            source.skip(length.toLong())
          }
          else -> throw ProtocolException("Unexpected field encoding: $groupOrFieldEncoding")
        }
      }
      throw EOFException("Expected a containing end group but reached the end of the input")
    }

    internal companion object {
      internal const val RECURSION_LIMIT = 100
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1954: a braced when arm's call is analysed"
  lang kotlin
  file wire-runtime/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/squareup/wire/ProtoReader.kt
  expect VYQL-RES-001
  code
  ```
  import java.io.FileInputStream

  class Importer {
    fun open(kind: Int, name: String) {
      when (kind) {
        1 -> { FileInputStream(name) }
        else -> 0
      }
    }
  }
  ```

